{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now boots with audit=1 persistently. After a safe reboot, the boot ID changed, the live kernel command line contains audit=1, kernel auditing reports enabled=1, and the system fully recovered. The OS release and kernel were preserved.","actions_performed":["Added audit=1 to all installed boot entries with grubby.","Preserved a root-owned mode-600 rollback backup at /root/grub.default.before-audit1.20261004T180350Z.","Safely rebooted node1 and removed the temporary reboot acknowledgement file.","Verified systemd is running, the root filesystem is read-write, and no units failed."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistently configure node1 to boot with audit=1","command_ids":["cmd-337e790a752e4f32","cmd-acee7aa2289e4e4c","cmd-c6c326bcddcf4ee6"],"summary":"Both normal and rescue boot entries contain audit=1. Following reboot, /proc/cmdline contains exactly one audit=1 parameter and auditctl reports enabled=1."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-61aeabeb7d744615","cmd-acee7aa2289e4e4c"],"summary":"Before and after the change, the system remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c574c41e17ec429c","cmd-915e76785e45462e","cmd-0a8bc3bb68c44256","cmd-acee7aa2289e4e4c","cmd-c6c326bcddcf4ee6"],"summary":"The healthy pre-restart boot ID was 636556ce-a308-49cc-b873-62cedb1c077d; the reboot was acknowledged; the recovered node reported boot ID 1b9b02f0-5951-45a6-b49d-8e51b0ca5d9b. Post-restart system state is running, the root filesystem is read-write, and failed-unit count is zero."}]}
